A Rust implementation of `dissect.cstruct`, built for `target-query` throughput.

## Install

```bash
gh release download @TAG@ --repo @REPO@ --pattern '*.whl' --pattern 'SHA256SUMS'
sha256sum --check --ignore-missing SHA256SUMS
gh attestation verify dissect_cstruct-*.whl --repo @REPO@

/path/to/dissect-env/bin/python -m pip install \
  --force-reinstall --no-deps dissect_cstruct-*.whl
```

This wheel uses upstream's distribution name and replaces it in the environment.
Install one implementation or the other, never both. `build_info()` reports which
one is active.

## Requirements

- CPython 3.13
- Linux x86-64-v3 or newer (AVX2, BMI2, FMA), checked at import
- glibc 2.28 or newer (`manylinux_2_28`)

## Dependency pins

`@VERSION@` resolves as `@PUBLIC@`; the local `+rs2.N` segment is ignored by
dependency solving. It satisfies `dissect.cstruct>=@MAJOR@,<@NEXT_MAJOR@` and
`>=@MAJOR@.0.dev,<@NEXT_MAJOR@.0.dev`. See the README for the full table and for
which upstream line this release tracks.

